  "name": "Sworn to the Saddle",
  "type": "feat",
  "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-worn-brown.webp",
  "system": {
    "description": "You are bound to a destrier: a warhorse, or something stranger from the deep stables, scaled or feathered or without a name the Order will speak aloud. Whatever its shape, it uses the Destrier stat block below. It is a permanent Moderate minion and counts toward your minion limit. While you ride it, you move it with your own Move actions as a mount (see Subsystem: Vehicles), and command it (◈) only to make it attack or use its active ability. In the saddle, you attack at normal speed without the +2 DR for attacking from a moving mount, and you ignore the Agility and defence penalties of armour up to tier 3 (tier 4 still defends at +2 DR). If your destrier dies, you can bind yourself to a new one only by raising or breaking it during Downtime (a horse costs 80 s; stranger beasts cost what the Dark Master asks).",
